hout First Nations presence repeats erasure."],"question":"Which task best shows independent use of colony?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating colony on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original response on new material: First Nations Peoples already lived there; the date marks British colonial government, not the start of human history. Reasoning: I used colony by attending to Australia rather than copying the worked model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason.","question":"Name one likely error with colony, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Common error: Learning colony names without First Nations presence repeats erasure. Correction: First Nations Peoples already lived there; the date marks British colonial government, not the start of human history. Why: the correction restores accurate use of colony.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent evidence and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-hsie-y4-w09-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA HSIE alignment using catalogue outcome codes (HS2-*); content-point mapping and local First Nations protocols remain pending human review.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise colony.","Read the mission before you start mapping or using sources.","Keep the place, people or source you are studying in view."],"guided":["